{"schema_version":1,"scope":"california-native-bag-sector-review-leads","generated_at":"2026-09-24T05:40:39.771560+00:00","audit_collected_at":"2026-09-23T22:19:40.733168+00:00","discovery_collected_at":"2026-09-23T18:33:06.148529+00:00","max_audited_file_bytes":100000000,"audited_bag_files":291,"audited_georeferenced_bag_files":289,"audit_health":{"status":"degraded","issues":["https://data.ngdc.noaa.gov/platforms/ocean/nos/coast/F00001-F02000/F00834/BAG/F00834_MB_VR_MLLW_2of2.bag","https://data.ngdc.noaa.gov/platforms/ocean/nos/coast/H12001-H14000/H13549/BAG/H13549_MB_VR_MLLW_1of1.bag"]},"method":"Intersect each original BAG geographic bounding box with the exact NOAA discovery request envelope for each browse sector, then count strictly reviewed regular-grid, substrate-screen and variable-resolution metadata leads separately. Survey-catalog associations alone do not count as in-sector grids.","reviewed_lead_holds":[{"survey_id":"F00562","reason":"This is a 2008 Crescent City harbor and approach survey. Its descriptive report identifies significant channel shoaling, numerous uncharted rocks along the southern offshore edge, and incomplete full-bottom coverage of the approach. The five eligible 4 m screen cells overlapping a predicted-hard polygon (about 80 square meters) cannot establish a natural fishing reef or a safe approach. Keep the survey for harbor-source review; do not promote it to a fishing target without a current chart, site-specific original-cell review and separate substrate evidence.","report_url":"https://data.ngdc.noaa.gov/platforms/ocean/nos/coast/F00001-F02000/F00562/DR/F00562.pdf","report_sha256":"d3918c40678662bf91b52ecf05cdb364dd0e34a69132c37845e1cd8acdc036e5"},{"survey_id":"H11967","reason":"The 2009 Stil Well Point\u2013Greenwood Cove survey contains fine measured depth and historical rocky-camera overlap, but its original report identifies five dangers to navigation, charted rocks/islets needing correction, and holidays where least depths were not established. The NOAA NBS sample has 60 locally qualified rocky-camera windows, yet only 18 also pass the strict 25 m original-BAG native-grid and depth screen; 37 are held at original fine-grid edges. Do not promote a Fort Bragg\u2013Point Arena target until hazards are reconciled with the current ENC, exact source footprints and position uncertainty are reviewed, and local species/method rules and access pass separately.","report_url":"https://data.ngdc.noaa.gov/platforms/ocean/nos/coast/H10001-H12000/H11967/DR/H11967.pdf","report_sha256":"02fae1f4b1fd7cb42cc8ffbfb06135a7ff8ac660d002c950f9c1988d6afcc96c"},{"survey_id":"H11972","reason":"The 2008\u20132009 Point Delgada original survey is the measured contributor behind a North Mendocino NOAA NBS test tile with 46 historical rocky-camera windows passing the local source screen. Its final descriptive report identifies seven dangers to navigation, two rocks of unknown depth placed over survey holidays on shoals shallower than four fathoms, revisions to charted islets and more extensive submerged rock than formerly charted. Dynamic sediment bottom also changed between the two acquisition periods. Withhold the whole survey as a fishing-target source until the original fine BAG cells, current ENC hazards, exact substrate and MPA footprints, access and Mendocino rules are reconciled. The tile and 2010 camera records alone do not locate a present fishable reef.","report_url":"https://data.ngdc.noaa.gov/platforms/ocean/nos/coast/H10001-H12000/H11972/DR/H11972.pdf","report_sha256":"06cbdbe11697666659a3465ec9161c19e36316825985df4f5844e9d45cc1cae7"}],"limitations":["A geographic bounding box includes unsurveyed water; these counts are not area coverage.","Only MLLW-named BAG files within the selected download size were audited; other NOAA surveys and USGS sources remain outside this count.","Variable-resolution native refinements need a separate cell-level compiler; a coarse BAG overview is not proof of poor native 